  "summary": "TIEM2 is Texas Instruments' second assembly and test factory in Melaka, Malaysia, a six-storey building connected to the existing Melaka plant. Announced in June 2023 with a potential investment of up to MYR 5 billion while already under construction, it opened in November 2025 and is in production, handling bump, probe, assembly and test of analog and embedded chips. It is part of TI's aim to bring most assembly and test work in house by 2030.",
